# Dual 24 GB GPU model set — 2× RTX 3090 / 2× RTX 4090 / similar (48 GB total, tp=2)
# Format: <short-name>  [<gguf-file>]  [<params>]  [hf:<tokenizer-repo>]
#
# This file is the standalone tp=2 counterpart to the dual-GPU section of default.vllm.
# Use it when running only dual-GPU models without the single-GPU 14B/32B entries.
#
# Context vs. single-GPU 32B (32gb.vllm):
#   tp=2 distributes KV cache across both GPUs → roughly double the KV budget.
#   qwen2.5-coder:32b: max_model_len 8192 (24 GB sg) → 65536 (tp=2, 48 GB)
#   deepseek-r1:32b:   max_model_len 8192 (24 GB sg) → 32768 (tp=2, 48 GB)
#   qwq:32b:           unusable (6 tok/s thrash on sg) → max_model_len=32768 (tp=2)
#   llama3.3:70b:      requires tp=2 minimum — does not fit on a single 24 GB GPU
#
# Run with:
#   ./run.sh --backend vllm --model-file models/2x24gb.vllm --models llama3.3:70b
#   ./compare.sh --backend vllm --model-file models/2x24gb.vllm

# ── 70B — primary tp=2 target; minimum 2× 24 GB ──────────────────────────────
# Q4_K_S (~37 GiB across 2 GPUs); proven at max_model_len=32768 on 2× RTX 3090.
# Tokenizer is gated (meta-llama) — set HF_TOKEN env var or populate hf-token.txt.
llama3.3:70b  Llama-3.3-70B-Instruct-Q4_K_S.gguf  tp=2,dtype=auto,max_model_len=32768  hf:meta-llama/Llama-3.3-70B-Instruct

# ── 32B models — tp=2 removes the single-GPU KV constraint ───────────────────
# qwen2.5-coder:32b: 10 GiB/GPU for weights → ~13 GiB KV total → max_model_len=65536
qwen2.5-coder:32b  Qwen2.5-Coder-32B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.gguf  tp=2,dtype=auto,max_model_len=65536  hf:Qwen/Qwen2.5-Coder-32B-Instruct
# deepseek-r1:32b: thinking; 10 GiB/GPU → with fp8 KV, ~26 GiB KV budget → try max_model_len=65536
# fp8 KV halves the KV footprint; verify python_hashmap does not regress before committing
deepseek-r1:32b  DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-32B-Q4_K_M.gguf  tp=2,dtype=auto,max_model_len=65536,kv_cache_dtype=fp8,enable_prefix_caching,thinking  hf:deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-32B
# qwq:32b Q5_K_M: ~11 GiB/GPU for weights → ~13 GiB KV total → max_model_len=32768
qwq:32b  QwQ-32B-Q5_K_M.gguf  tp=2,dtype=auto,max_model_len=32768,thinking  hf:Qwen/QwQ-32B

# ── Qwen3-Coder-30B-A3B comparison: GGUF Q4_K_M vs AWQ ──────────────────────
# GGUF mode: requires patched vLLM using --quantization gguf (not --load-format gguf).
# CONFIRMED 2026-07-06 at tp=1 single 4090: 15/16 eligible tasks PASS, 31.2 tok/s.
# KV ceiling single 24 GB: max_model_len=8192 (GGUF loader overhead ~5 GB; estimated max ~13760).
# tp=2 here: expect ~13-17 tok/s from PCIe all-reduce overhead (same as AWQ tp=2 at 16.6 tok/s).
# dtype=float16 required for MoE GGUF plugin (not auto). enforce_eager avoids CUDA graph overhead.
# hf: field is the base model tokenizer repo (not the GGUF quant repo).
qwen3-coder:30b-gguf  Qwen3-Coder-30B-A3B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.gguf  tp=2,dtype=float16,enforce_eager,gpu_mem_util=0.88,max_model_len=32768  hf:Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-30B-A3B-Instruct
# AWQ Int4 — Ampere+Ada compatible via awq_marlin. fp8 arm dead on 4090+3090 TP:
# both W8A8 variants (Qwen official + BCCard FP8-Dynamic) quantize activations to E4M3 (fp8e4nv);
# RTX 3090 (Ampere) cannot do this and there is no Marlin fallback for block-scaled fp8 in TP.
# cpatonn variant chosen over QuantTrio — QuantTrio may trigger vLLM Mamba/SSM misdetection.
# Downloaded automatically to ~/.cache/huggingface/hub/ on first vllm serve call.
qwen3-coder:30b-awq  -  tp=2,gpu_mem_util=0.88,enforce_eager,enable_prefix_caching,max_model_len=32768  hf:cpatonn/Qwen3-Coder-30B-A3B-Instruct-AWQ-4bit
